## End of Material Changes section.

Eight verified material changes documented. None require restructuring of D4 substructure or aggregate-finding architecture; all are either date-precision refinements, additional substantive details, or new substantive developments since draft date that strengthen rather than disrupt the second-pass framing. The MAHA-era three-pattern co-occurrence (rule withdrawals + capacity erosion + data-infrastructure rollback) framing is reinforced by MC-V-3 (additional NRTE delay), MC-V-7 (per-Center RIF detail + Rhode Island injunction), and MC-V-8 (announcement-date precision + advocate framing of cost rationale). The Philadelphia paradox (G1-SD4-01 = G1-XC-05) is quantitatively confirmed by MC-V-5 with low US-wide uptake data.


