## §1. Data Provenance

The SD1 pass2 record draws from: 36 first-pass sources covering FFDCA Chapter IV statutory architecture (FDA), FSMA implementation, DSHEA dietary supplement regime, FALCPA / FASTER allergen labeling, MoCRA cosmetics implementation, federal SNAP / WIC / NSLP architecture, PA Food Safety Act, Philadelphia Code Title 6 Chapter 6-300, PDPH OFP operations, PDPH Get Healthy Philly + Healthy Corner Store Initiative + Food Bucks, plus Census ACS PA-3 demographics and USDA-ERS food security reporting baseline (final 2024 edition).

Directly documented [D]: federal statutory citations; FDA Philadelphia District (Mellon Independence Center) location; PDPH OFP licensure structure; SNAP FY25 maximum benefit; 21.2% regional food insecurity (Greater Philadelphia FI baseline); 36.9% household FI in studied North Philadelphia tracts; corner-store unit-price premium 10-30%. Structurally derivable [SD]: PA-3 sub-area inspection density variation (PADHS / PDPH retrieval target F4-T2P2-SD1-2 P2); PA-3 sub-area FI direct disaggregation (target F4-T2P2-SD1-1 P1). Structurally inferred [SI]: hair-product chemical-exposure pathway for Black PA-3 women cosmetics consumers (deepening target F4-T2P2-SD1-3 P1; peer-reviewed literature retrieval). Continuing currency caveat: USDA ERS Household Food Security report series terminated with 2024 edition — the data infrastructure characterizing the very pattern T2P2 depends on is itself eroded.

