## §1. Data Provenance

The SD2 record draws from FMIA / PPIA / EPIA statutory architecture; USDA FSIS Pathogen Reduction / HACCP Final Rule (1996); FSIS Salmonella Framework for Raw Poultry Products (proposed 2024; **withdrawn April 25, 2025; 90 FR 17344**); FMIA ritual-slaughter provision (21 U.S.C. § 1902); PA Food Safety Act + PA Retail Food Facility Safety Act; Philadelphia Code Title 6 §6-301 USDA jurisdictional carve-out at retail; PDPH OFP retail-level enforcement.

Directly documented [D]: federal statutory citations; FSIS Philadelphia District 60 location at Mellon Independence Center; April 25, 2025 Salmonella Framework withdrawal; Salmonella national illness baseline (~1.35M cases/year per CDC FoodNet); ~25% of foodborne Salmonella illness was within scope of withdrawn framework; PA non-cooperative MPI status; April 2025 USDA workforce reductions (11,300+ deferred resignations effective).

Structurally derivable [SD]: PA-3-specific Salmonella incidence (national rate × population × demographic exposure profile; F4-T2P2-SD2-1 P1 direct disaggregation target); halal / kosher retailer count by sub-area (F4-T2P2-SD2-3 P1 retrieval target); FSIS Philadelphia District 60 staffing actuals post-2025 USDA workforce reductions (F4-T2P2-SD2-2 P2).

Currency caveat: January 2026 FSIS public meeting on Salmonella regulatory pathway — replacement-tool status pending verification at execution date.

