Sources include: FFDCA Chapter IX (Family Smoking Prevention and Tobacco Control Act 2009 — TCA); TCA implementing regulations including premarket tobacco product application (PMTA) framework; menthol withdrawal RIN 0910-AI60 (January 2025); characterizing-flavors-in-cigars rule withdrawal; PA Act 14 of 2020 (PA Tobacco 21; effective July 1, 2020); PA Clean Indoor Air Act; Philadelphia Code Title 6 Chapter 6-700 (Sale of Tobacco Products); Title 10 Chapter 10-700; PDPH tobacco enforcement architecture; documented SNAP-authorized retailer interior advertising 3.43x pattern in compound-disadvantage sub-areas.

[D]: TCA statutory framework; menthol withdrawal date and RIN; CTP Office of Regulations April 2025 RIF ("entire office responsible for drafting new tobacco regulations" RIF documented); CTP user-fee FY26 funding stability; PA Tobacco 21 effective date; Title 6 §6-700 1-per-1,000 retailer density cap + 500-foot school buffer architecture; documented SNAP-authorized retailer interior advertising 3.43x pattern. [SD]: PA-3 sub-area tobacco marketing density (F4-T2P2-SD5-1 P1 retrieval target); menthol smoking prevalence by PA-3 sub-area + race (F4-T2P2-SD5-3 P2). Currency caveat: post-CTP RIF replacement-tool development pathway functionally absent — Office of Regulations capacity decimated.

