## §3. Supporting prose

The SD5 chain shows a single constitutional pathway: Commerce Clause regulation through TCA 2009 federal architecture, with state (PA Act 14; PA CIAA) and local (Title 6 §6-700; Title 10 §10-700) overlays operating concurrently. Inline labeling: TCA carries HIGH statutory stability (bipartisan 2009 enactment) [D]. **CTP carries EXTREME administrative vulnerability — singular among D4 sub-domains** — the April 2025 Office of Regulations RIF documented as "the entire office responsible for drafting new tobacco regulations" decimating regulatory-development capacity [D, XC-9 timestamp]. The user-fee funding stability documented through FY26 [D] does not substitute for regulatory-development workforce capacity; CTP can continue to conduct PMTA review and retail enforcement on user-fee revenue, but new regulation development is functionally absent post-RIF.

PADoH carries MODERATE administrative vulnerability (state capacity stable). PDPH carries MODERATE administrative vulnerability (local capacity stable; sub-area enforcement density variation flagged F4-T2P2-SD5-1 P1).

Anchor institution analysis: the structural-actor anchor at SD5 is PDPH at the retail enforcement + density-cap administration layer; engagement scoring HIGH at the local-layer dimension. The XC-11 differential at SD5 is concentrated: small tobacco retailers operate under the density cap + 500-foot school buffer + license fee architecture differentially against corporate-chain retailers whose compliance infrastructure absorbs regulatory burden differently. Documented SNAP-authorized retailer interior advertising 3.43x pattern in compound-disadvantage sub-areas concentrates at small retailers — the marketing density pattern operates at the small-retailer layer and produces disparate marketing exposure at the PA-3 sub-area level [D].

---

## §4. Statistical profile

National menthol baseline: ~85% of Black smokers use menthol vs. ~30% of white smokers [D, broader literature]; menthol cigarettes documented as a primary contributor to Black smoking-related mortality differential [D]; FDA menthol cigarette ban proposed rulemaking originated in 2022 with disparate-impact remediation rationale.

National menthol withdrawal status: **Menthol cigarette ban withdrawn January 2025** (RIN 0910-AI60) [D]; characterizing-flavors-in-cigars rule withdrawn [D]; preamble of menthol proposed rule contained explicit disparate-impact citations (F4-T2P2-SD5-2 P1 retrieval target — direct preamble citation retrieval).

PA-3 specific baseline: documented Black smoking prevalence elevated relative to white; menthol concentration among Black smokers structurally consequential for smoking-related mortality at PA-3 Black population level [SD; national pattern × PA-3 demographics]. PA-3 sub-area smoking prevalence and menthol-specific data at sub-area resolution flagged F4-T2P2-SD5-3 P2.

PA-3 tobacco retail infrastructure: PDPH 1-per-1,000 density cap operative since [D — date of cap implementation]; current retailer count + density compliance pattern by sub-area flagged F4-T2P2-SD5-1 P1; 500-foot school buffer operative architecture; retailer revocation provisions operative.

PA-3 marketing density: documented SNAP-authorized retailer interior advertising 3.43x pattern in compound-disadvantage sub-areas (relative to non-compound-disadvantage sub-areas) [D]; marketing concentration at small retailers in N./Northwest Phila Core + portions of W. Phila Core + S. Phila operates structurally on Black PA-3 menthol-smoker pathway.

CTP enforcement capacity: April 2025 Office of Regulations RIF — "entire office responsible for drafting new tobacco regulations" decimated [D]; user-fee FY26 funding stability documented [D]; PMTA review and retail enforcement continuing on user-fee revenue; new-regulation development functionally absent.

---

## §5. Geographic variation across four sub-areas

**North/Northwest Philadelphia Core** [D]: highest documented marketing-density concentration; SNAP-authorized retailer interior advertising 3.43x pattern most acute; predominantly Black sub-area; documented elevated menthol smoking prevalence concentration; small-retailer concentration concentrated.

**West Philadelphia Core** [D]: significant marketing-density concentration in compound-disadvantage portions; Cobbs Creek-area Black population concentration; small-retailer marketing concentration documented.

**Northwest Philadelphia (Mt. Airy)** [SD]: lower marketing-density concentration; mixed-income demographic; lower menthol smoking prevalence concentration.

**South/Southwest Philadelphia** [D]: marketing-density concentration in compound-disadvantage portions; documented Rite Aid pharmacy desert closure concentration (cross-ref SD3) reduces cessation pharmacotherapy access vector (G1-SD5-05); small-retailer concentration variable by corridor.

Sub-area summary: SNAP-authorized retailer interior advertising 3.43x pattern concentrates in compound-disadvantage sub-areas (N./Northwest Phila Core + portions of W. Phila Core + S. Phila); the marketing pattern operates at small-retailer layer differentially; the pattern that the withdrawn menthol rule would have substantively addressed concentrates in the PA-3 sub-areas where Black population concentration is highest [D].

