## §4. Statistical profile

National OUD baseline: ~7-8% U.S. population with substance use disorder; ~2.5M with OUD specifically [D, broader literature]; methadone-vs-buprenorphine racial-pattern asymmetry documented (methadone access concentrated at clinics; buprenorphine access concentrated at office-based prescribers; documented racial pattern in distribution) [D].

Philadelphia OUD baseline: documented Kensington compound-incidence locus with multi-substance concentration — medetomidine 83% of Philadelphia drug supply by March 2025 [D, Source 33]; BTMPS 25% [D, Source 34]; xylazine continued co-occurrence [D, Source 32]; documented overdose mortality decline ~24% from 2022 peak [D, broader Philadelphia mortality reporting]. **Both-true framing critical**: overdose mortality decline + Mayor Parker ecosystem expansion + structurally entrenched compound factors all operate simultaneously; the decline is real and the entrenchment is real; the second pass preserves both.

Prevention Point demographics: 62% white / 26% Black / 83% unhoused [D, Source 35]; structurally entrenched parallel-infrastructure engagement pattern at the primary harm-reduction anchor.

PA-3 specific OUD baseline: PA-3 OUD prevalence at PA-3 sub-area resolution flagged F4-T2P2-SD6-3 P2; Kensington geography intersects PA-3 boundary partially (specific tract analysis pending verification); cross-cut SD3 G1-SD3-04 buprenorphine prescriber density and pharmacy availability gap.

PA medical marijuana baseline: ~430,000 PA medical marijuana patients (PA DoH Office of Medical Marijuana published baseline) [D]; PA-3 specific patient count by sub-area flagged for direct retrieval (cross-cut state-level data); ~190 PA dispensaries; PA-3 dispensary count flagged F4-T2P2-SD6-2 P1.

DEA Schedule III implementation baseline: today-effective Final Order; 60-day priority window through June 22, 2026; DEA registration pathway for medical marijuana licensees newly operative; PA-3 dispensary registration uptake during 60-day window flagged.

Mayor Parker ecosystem: $100M+ wellness ecosystem expansion documented; mobile fentanyl treatment unit scope; expanded harm-reduction architecture across multiple Philadelphia sub-areas including Kensington-area concentration.

PA controlled substance prescriber baseline (cross-ref SD3): MAT Act 2022 expanded prescribing eligibility ~3,000-4,000 PA-3 prescriber-eligible cadre [SD; structural inference]; suspicious-order monitoring constraint operative under DEA Diversion Control architecture.

