## §9. Representation Question (synthesis-level)

**Element 1 — Formal provision (synthesis composite).** SD7 synthesizes federal-state-local architecture across SD1-SD6: foundational federal statutes operative (HIGH stability composite); state architectures (PA Food Safety Act; PA Tobacco 21; PA CIAA; PA Drug Act; PA Medical Marijuana Act; PA Act 77 of 2024 PBM reform; ABC-MAP; PA Pharmacy Act; PA Retail Food Facility Safety Act; etc.); local architecture (Title 6 Chapters 6-300, 6-301, 6-700, 10-700; PDPH OFP + Get Healthy Philly + Healthy Corner Store + Food Bucks; Division of Disease Control; tobacco enforcement; DBHIDS).

**Element 2 — Actual receipt (synthesis composite).** Federal-cluster simultaneity producing 5 of 6 SDs at HIGH or EXTREME admin vulnerability; three-pattern co-occurrence (rule withdrawal + capacity erosion + data-infrastructure rollback) operating heterogeneously across SDs; today-effective Schedule III at SD6 alone documenting expansion direction; XC-11 differential burden at small / independent organization layer across all SDs; Compound Disadvantage Geography Matrix documenting simultaneous concentration in N./Northwest Phila Core + portions of W. Phila Core + S. Phila.

**Element 3 — Account for the gap (synthesis composite).** Three structurally co-occurring patterns at SD7 synthesis level: (a) federal-cluster simultaneity across multiple agencies; (b) three-pattern co-occurrence (rule withdrawal / capacity erosion / data-infrastructure rollback); (c) XC-11 independent / small organization differential burden as additional structurally-co-occurring pattern. The gap is not a function of architecture absence — the architecture nominally provides comprehensive coverage. The gap is a function of architecture *operational reach* eroding across multiple federal agencies simultaneously, withdrawn or vacated rules at substantive disparate-impact-remediation availability points, and structurally entrenched compound-disadvantage geography concentration that the architecture does not directly reach.

**Element 4 — Meaning for representation analysis (synthesis composite).** SD7's synthesis shows that D4's representation gap operates not through any single SD's architecture failure but through compound architecture stress: federal-cluster simultaneity + three-pattern co-occurrence + XC-11 differential + compound-disadvantage geography concentration operating simultaneously at PA-3 sub-area level. The defining D4 representation paradoxes are: **the Philadelphia paradox** at SD4 (cell/gene therapy ATC concentration at University City + documented elevated SCD prevalence in adjacent sub-areas + low uptake; G1-SD4-01 = G1-XC-05); **the IRA MFP / pharmacy desert intersection** at SD3 (federal pricing protection effective + ~20% PA pharmacy reduction simultaneous; G1-SD3-02); **the foreclosed-remediation pattern** at SD5 (menthol withdrawal + CTP Office of Regulations RIF; G1-SD5-01 = G1-XC-08). All three paradoxes co-occur at SD7 synthesis level + operate within compound-disadvantage geography simultaneously.

