## Unverified-Claims Section

The following claims were sought but not verified within the verification budget; retained with explicit notation.

### F4-T2P2-SD1-1 [UNVERIFIED — pending direct PADHS retrieval]
**Claim:** PA-3 sub-area food insecurity direct disaggregation.
**What was sought:** Sub-area-level FI data at PADHS (Pennsylvania Department of Human Services) or Feeding America Map the Meal Gap county-level extension.
**What prevented verification:** Sub-area disaggregation not directly retrievable via web search; requires direct PADHS data request or research-tier access.
**Disposition:** Retained with [SD] structural-derivation premise stated; F4-T2P2-SD1-1 P1 verification target carried forward to next verification cycle.

### F4-T2P2-SD2-3 [UNVERIFIED — pending direct PADA / PDPH OFP retrieval]
**Claim:** Halal / kosher retailer count by sub-area.
**What was sought:** PADA Bureau of Food Safety + PDPH OFP retail-licensing data on halal/kosher retailer count by Philadelphia sub-area.
**What prevented verification:** Retail-licensing data at sub-area resolution not directly published; requires direct PADA / PDPH OFP data request.
**Disposition:** Retained with [D] qualitative documentation of corridor concentration; F4-T2P2-SD2-3 P1 verification target carried forward.

### F4-T2P2-SD3-1 [UNVERIFIED at PA-3 sub-area level — verified at PA state level]
**Claim:** PA-3 pharmacy count by sub-area post-August 2025 closures.
**What was sought:** PA-3 sub-area pharmacy count + chain/independent mix + pharmacy desert tract count.
**What was verified:** PA-state-level ~20% pharmacy reduction confirmed; specific Rite Aid sub-area closures confirmed (9th Street/Italian Market; Grays Ferry; Aramingo Avenue; Eastwick; Woodland Avenue).
**What prevented verification:** Sub-area pharmacy count not directly indexed via web search; requires PA Pharmacy Board direct request.
**Disposition:** PA-3 state-level confirmed; sub-area-specific count carried forward to next verification cycle.

### F4-T2P2-SD4-1 [PARTIALLY VERIFIED — national level confirmed; Penn/CHOP institutional pending]
**Claim:** Casgevy/Lyfgenia uptake at Penn/CHOP for PA-3 SCD patients.
**What was verified:** US-wide Casgevy 64 + Lyfgenia ~100 cumulative through 2025 (substantially confirms low-uptake framing).
**What prevented verification:** Penn/CHOP institutional uptake reporting requires direct institutional retrieval.
**Disposition:** F4-T2P2-SD4-1 partially upgraded from P1 to P2 (national-level data adequately characterizes structural barriers; Penn/CHOP-specific data nice-to-have for next verification cycle).

### F4-T2P2-SD5-1 [UNVERIFIED — pending direct PDPH retail tobacco data]
**Claim:** PA-3 sub-area tobacco marketing density; retailer count + density compliance pattern by sub-area.
**What was sought:** PDPH retail tobacco license data at sub-area resolution; density-cap compliance pattern.
**What prevented verification:** Sub-area retail tobacco license data not directly indexed via web search; requires PDPH direct request.
**Disposition:** Citywide level confirmed (2.2/1,000 retailer density; PDPH density cap operative); sub-area-specific data carried forward.

### F4-T2P2-SD5-2 [UNVERIFIED — pending direct preamble retrieval]
**Claim:** Menthol withdrawal preamble disparate-impact citations.
**What was sought:** Direct retrieval of 2022 NPRM preamble disparate-impact data.
**What was verified:** Preamble exists; documented Black-community disparate-impact framing; ~85% of Black smokers use menthol.
**What prevented verification:** Direct preamble citations require Federal Register full-text retrieval; not surfaced via search.
**Disposition:** Qualitative confirmation adequate for current analysis; direct preamble citation retrieval carried forward (F4-T2P2-SD5-2 P1).

### F4-T2P2-SD6-1 [UNVERIFIED — pending PubMed retrieval]
**Claim:** Black PA-3 OUD-population engagement-pattern peer-reviewed lit.
**What was sought:** Peer-reviewed literature on Black PA-3 OUD-population engagement-pattern with traditional / peer-support / faith-based / family-community treatment infrastructure.
**What prevented verification:** PubMed search not conducted in this verification cycle; substantive literature retrieval requires dedicated academic database search.
**Disposition:** Critical careful framing (G1-SD6-02 — gap-finding without pathologizing) preserved through verified document; F4-T2P2-SD6-1 P1 carried forward.

### F4-T2P2-SD6-2 [PENDING — too early; window opened today]
**Claim:** DEA marijuana Schedule III medical-marijuana-licensee registration uptake first 60-day window.
**What was sought:** DEA Diversion Control reporting + PA DoH OMM registration uptake during 60-day priority window through ~June 27, 2026.
**What prevented verification:** Window opens today (April 29, 2026 at 9 AM EST); first-day data not yet available.
**Disposition:** F4-T2P2-SD6-2 P1 retained as forward-looking verification target; first-window status assessed at end of priority window.

### F4-T2P2-SD7-2 (CDC FoodNet PA-3 disaggregation portion) [UNVERIFIED]
**Claim:** CDC FoodNet PA-3 sub-area disaggregation absence.
**What was sought:** CDC FoodNet program reporting on PA-3 sub-area Salmonella incidence disaggregation.
**What prevented verification:** Direct CDC FoodNet program-status confirmation requires CDC-side retrieval.
**Disposition:** Continuing data-infrastructure-rollback framing preserved; F4-T2P2-SD7-2 PA-3 portion carried forward.

